        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:left&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Upgrade flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt; · Bump kubernetes_version by one minor version and open a PR.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt; · The PR runs validate and terraform-plan; merging runs terraform-apply and argocd-sync.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt; · Runners exchange a GitHub OIDC token for GitHubActionsEKSUpgradeRole credentials.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt; · Terraform reads and writes state in S3 with native locking.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt; · terraform apply upgrades the control plane over the public endpoint.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt; · The same apply then rolls the managed node group onto the new version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt; · argocd-sync opens kubectl port-forward to svc/argocd-server through the EKS API, then runs argocd app sync.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;8&lt;/b&gt; · ApplicationSets read cluster-config.yaml from Git.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;9&lt;/b&gt; · Applications render the desired-version ConfigMaps (selfHeal).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;10&lt;/b&gt; · The job publishes the result to Amazon SNS.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="570" width="310" x="20" y="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
